Google's board audio configuration is for a Lenovo SOF codec. The Lenovo E50-80's ALC233 uses
analog PCM 0 for the speaker, headphone, internal mic (pin 0x12) and jack mic (0x19), with the
HDA jack input devices named by its "HDA Intel PCH" card. Unmute the HDA mixer; keep Google's
neutral DSP graph and volume curves. HDMI audio is on a separate card and is omitted.
These are copies of Google's files in this laptop's own directory, bind-mounted over the board
directory at boot, because the MSI patches the board directory in place.
Drop when Google supports this laptop.

